-- title:
--   §4.2 — derived-field and total-instance bit growth
-- statement:
--   There is an absolute $C>0$, chosen before every graph and spin count, such that every instance $\Phi_\omega$ obtained from positive rational $\Phi$ by the source’s outer pinnings and child removals satisfies, for each remaining vertex $u$,
--   $$\operatorname{bit}(\lambda^{(\omega)}_u)\le C\left(\operatorname{bit}(\lambda_u)+\sum_{e\in E(G)\setminus E(G_\omega),\,u\in e}\operatorname{bit}(A_e)\right),\qquad |\Phi_\omega|\le C|\Phi|.$$
--   Vector and matrix lengths sum the binary lengths of their entries. Derived instances are generated by actual single-vertex pin or child operations; the hypotheses do not supply the desired bit bounds.
--
--   The item retains the displayed per-field estimate and its total-encoding consequence on p. 18.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: finite ordered vertex and spin sets → Fin n and Fin q, with an active vertex subset; reason: relabeling preserves every instance; active subsets implement the source sub-instances and the fixed vertex order
--   - encoding: O(·) with an absolute implicit constant → one positive natural constant chosen before all inputs and dimensions; reason: the finitely many small encoding sizes are absorbed in this constant; no input is excluded
--   - encoding: sequences of outer pinnings and recursive calls → the inductive reachability relation generated by exactly those operations at active vertices; reason: each deletion removes the vertex permanently, so an original edge contributes at most once
--   - generalization: q ≥ 3 in the counting theorem → every q ≥ 1, including empty derived instances; reason: rational product bit lengths obey the same bound for each of these cases and include the source domain
-- source:
--   Zhidan Li, Kuan Yang, STOC 2027 submission #268 (October 2026), pp. 17–18, §4.2, unnumbered bit-length display and following sentence

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MultiSpinCounting_Positive_Encoding

namespace MultiSpinCounting.Positive

/-- §4.2, pp. 17--18. The relation Derived only permits the source's pin/removal steps. -/
theorem derived_bit_growth :
    ∃ C : ℕ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ (n q : ℕ), 0 < q → ∀ (Φ Ψ : Instance n q ℚ),
      IsPositive Φ → Derived Φ Ψ →
      (∀ u ∈ Ψ.active,
        vectorBits (Ψ.field u) ≤ C*(vectorBits (Φ.field u) +
          ∑ e ∈ (edges Φ \ edges Ψ).filter (fun e => e.1 = u ∨ e.2 = u),
            matrixBits (Φ.interaction e.1 e.2))) ∧
      (encInstance Ψ).length ≤ C*(encInstance Φ).length := by sorry

end MultiSpinCounting.Positive
